title Caravan concurrent -- two children of one ring at once, and the pair of tests a document must pass
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the finished increment.
think Standfast first. Read crux/REDS.md whole: every living row carries a closure note, #85 reopened-and-closed on 20260819.134229 with its loom standing, #84 closed on measurement, #87 released. No open agent-closable red, so the constructive queue is clear rather than routed around.
think Running thread from session-logs/README.md row 1 -- inflight.rye named its own next crux exactly: more than one lap in flight at once, whether two children of the same ring may run concurrently, and what a document owes a supervisor holding two unreaped outcomes rather than one. The lap is filled from the record rather than invented.
think Council rota by lap index -- 464 .kyri logs on disk, this is lap 465, and 465 mod 27 = 6, so the deep-read was foundations/20260814-071700_hardware-and-right-to-repair.md. Its shape governed how this rung states itself: the season front door proves each promise as a load-bearing invariant in code rather than a claim, so the concurrency rule here is derived from the declaration and refused on metal rather than described.
think The crux, before any code. Concurrency in this arc could have been a supervisor policy -- a list of domains the parent happens to run together. That would be a schedule, and the arc has been retiring schedules one ring at a time. So the question was pushed into the document: what does a declaration already say about which two of its domains may hold the ring at one moment?
think The memory half was already on the shelf. relay.share_a_region derived the two ends of a chain sharing nothing, which is the isolation a relay rests on; the same predicate answers concurrency exactly. Reuse over restatement -- no new derivation was written for a question an existing one answers.
think The doorbell half is the finding the memory half hides. A bell is state: one side rings it, the other hears and clears it, so two children racing on one counter is the same hazard one layer up. Channels are declared apart from grants, so a document may wire two domains that share no memory at all, and a test reading only the grants would wave that pair through.
think Proving both tests load-bearing needed two mirror documents, and building them surfaced something sharper than planned. Inside a true ring the two tests always agree, because a region joining two domains makes them neighbors -- so the region test alone is unprovable within a ring. serial_cycle_wide_mute.bron earns its silent sharing by ceasing to be a ring, the same price serial_cycle_bypass.bron paid for a spare route. The separation of the tests costs the shape, and that is stated rather than hidden.
think A ring of three has no concurrency at all, and that is arithmetic rather than a limitation of the module. Every domain in a ring is adjacent to two others, so the pairs left over number n*(n-3)/2 -- zero at three, two at four. serial_cycle.bron was entirely serial by its own grants, which is why the rung needed a wider ring rather than a cleverer supervisor.
think The second half of inflight's lesson gained an edge here. With one child standing, an abandoned child was a leak dressed as a safety check; with two in flight the first outcome may be a refusal, and reporting it the instant it arrives leaves a sibling running behind the verdict. The unsafe reading stands in the module as a named Reaping.first_only control, so the safe reading is proven against it rather than asserted.
obs Both RED probes proven load-bearing on metal before the green was claimed. With the region test disabled the mute pair read back as safe -- a store shared in silence waved through. With the channel test disabled the wired pair read back the same way. Neither refusal is a rule the module enforces; both are the declaration, read back.
obs Real concurrency is visible in the output rather than only counted: the two children of a stage interleave their prints differently between runs, so every witness check is order-independent by construction.
obs The reaping probe's children carry a plan whose shape their verb does not take, so each is refused at its own door and neither touches a region or a bell. The probe measures the reaping alone, and the ring's state after it stands exactly where the lap left it.
obs A first cut of run_stage came to 73 lines, past the tame_style_check 70-line ratchet. Split at its natural seam -- clear_pair judges the document before any spawn, run_stage holds only the spawning and the reaping. The seam reads better than the length rule asked for.
obs Twenty-five green-witnessed Rye rings now carry the Microkit shape across real processes. TAME surface GREEN -- tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, the apostrophe loom GREEN, living-docs lint advisory only.
loom witness=caravan_concurrent_witness children=10 stages=8 concurrent_stages=2 peak_in_flight=2 reaped=10 unreaped_at_report=0 asks_home=4 pairs_ring3=0 pairs_ring4=2
file caravan/concurrent.rye the rung -- the pairing derived from grants and wiring, the stage of two, the reaping owed before any verdict
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle_wide.bron a ring of four, the first shape in the arc with room in it
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle_wide_wired.bron one bare channel across a region-disjoint pair, so the grants alone would clear it
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle_wide_mute.bron the mirror -- a store shared in silence, which the channels alone would clear
file tools/caravan_concurrent_witness.rish the witness, GREEN on metal, every check order-independent
file caravan/README.md the ladder row and the section that reads the finding without the code
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge condensed forward and the git nib pinned in the work commit
recommend keep-going The next crux is what the ring cannot answer yet -- concurrency here is bounded at a pair because a ring of four has no non-adjacent triple, so the honest next question is a shape with room for three at once, and whether a supervisor derives the widest set it may run rather than the widest pair.
